{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Elohei your father.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, revealed Himself to Jacob in the language that honored him, as it is written: ״ויזבח זבחים לאלקי אביו יצחק״ (and he offered sacrifices to the Elohim of his father Isaac)." "<b>Do not fear going down to Egypt.</b> One says 'do not fear' only to one who is afraid, for Jacob was afraid and said: now that I am going down to Egypt, the days draw near that were decreed upon the elders — the decree of bondage and affliction upon my seed in a land not theirs. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: <b>do not fear going down to Egypt.</b> To your father I gave warning when I came to you it was to assure you: if the days of bondage and affliction have drawn near, the blessing that I blessed your elders has also drawn near — ״ואעשך לגוי גדול״ (and I will make you a great nation). That is the meaning of ״כי לגוי גדול אשימך שם״ (for a great nation I will make you there)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:45.475037245Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}